# Best Practices

When writing or editing code: follow current RN/Expo/TS best practices; refactor touched code; fix smells.

## TypeScript

- Explicit types; avoid `as` unless necessary; prefer unions/discriminated unions
- Extract shared types to `types/`

## React Native

- Correct hook dependency arrays; accessibilityLabel/Role on interactive elements
- Split large files (>500 lines); functions >50 lines → smaller units
- FlatList: stable keys, windowing, `getItemLayout` when useful
- Cache with AsyncStorage for offline (see `useDonation.ts`); debounce input handlers

## Errors & state

```typescript
// Good
try {
  setData(await fetchData());
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Failed to fetch data:', error);
  setError('Unable to load data. Please try again.');
}

// useEffect cleanup to avoid races
useEffect(() => {
  let isMounted = true;
  load().then((r) => { if (isMounted) setData(r); });
  return () => { isMounted = false; };
}, []);
```

## When modifying existing code

1. Fix lint warnings in that file  
2. Add missing types; extract magic values  
3. Add error handling; clarify names  
4. Remove unused imports/vars  

## Security

Never commit secrets/keystores. Validate input; do not put secrets in AsyncStorage; avoid leaking internals in errors.
